From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:22:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 72/76] ci: drop actions/setup-python and use the runner
 image's system Python (gcp-gtux)

actions/setup-python installs a portable CPython from actions/python-versions
that is built --enable-shared with no RPATH, so its bundled
libpython3.12.so.1.0 has to be registered with the dynamic linker to be
loadable. Registration writes to /etc/ld.so.conf.d and runs ldconfig, both of
which need root -- and the ARC runner container ends with `USER runner`
(uid 1001). Verified in a live pod: the interpreter and its library are both
on disk, ldconfig knows nothing about libpython, `ldd` reports
"libpython3.12.so.1.0 => not found", and the binary only runs when
LD_LIBRARY_PATH is set by hand. Every subsequent `python3 ...` step exited 127.

The image already ships system Python 3.12.3 at /usr/bin/python3, which
satisfies every `python-version: "3.12"` pin in the repo, so the fix is to stop
downloading a second interpreter rather than to work around the linker. On a
self-hosted runner, taking the toolchain from the image is the correct posture
-- the same principle as the Go half of gcp-k9cy, in the opposite direction:
Go is added to the image so workflows stop assuming an ambient toolchain;
Python's redundant downloader is removed so workflows stop fighting the one
already there. The image-side alternative (pre-seed /opt/hostedtoolcache and
run ldconfig at build time, as the hosted images do) is materially more work
and would still carry a second Python for no gain.

Removes the three-line `Set up Python` block at five sites -- ci.yml,
gascity-pack-inference.yml, pack-release-compatibility.yml, and both jobs in
supported-pack-nightly.yml -- and nothing else. The second nightly site also
carried `if: steps.subset.outputs.run_gate == 'true'`, which goes with the
step. No runs-on, step, or version changes.

Validation: all four files re-parse under yaml.safe_load; the diff is exactly
the five blocks and their trailing blank lines; local pre-flights green
(go vet, golangci-lint 0 issues, validate_registry.py ok, go test ok).

Follow-ups, not fixed here: the `python3 -m pip install` steps now run against
the system interpreter, so they depend on the image providing a usable pip
(PEP 668 marks Ubuntu 24.04's python3 externally-managed); this could not be
verified from the repo, which does not define the runner image. Separately,
pack-release-compatibility.yml still pins go-version "1.22" while ci.yml
resolves 1.25.9 from go.mod -- real skew, explicitly out of this bead's scope.
